page("smash-burgers-on-a-griddle-plate","Smash Burgers on a Collapsible Grill Griddle Plate","Crispy-edged smash burgers on a carbon steel griddle plate over charcoal, sized for a collapsible grill.","grid2",recipe(
"<p>Smash burgers need a screaming-hot flat surface, which is exactly what a carbon steel <a href='"+GRID+"'>griddle plate</a> over a bed of coals gives you. Thin patties, hard press, deep crust, done in minutes.</p>",
"4","25 minutes",["1 lb ground beef, 80/20","Salt and pepper","4 slices American cheese","4 soft buns, buttered","1 small onion, very thinly sliced (optional)","Pickles, mustard, sauce of choice"],
["Divide the beef into 8 loose balls (2 oz each). Keep them cold.","Light a full chimney and pour the coals under the griddle half. Put a grate on the other half for toasting buns.","Preheat the griddle 5 to 8 minutes, until a drop of water vanishes almost instantly. Wipe on a thin film of oil.","Place two or three balls on the griddle, spaced well apart. Smash each flat with a sturdy spatula (a second spatula pressing on top helps). Hold 10 seconds. Season.","Optional: press a pinch of onion into the top of each patty before flipping.","Cook about 2 minutes until the edges are deeply browned. Scrape under each patty and flip.","Add cheese and stack two patties per burger. Cook about 1 minute more, until cooked through to 160°F.","Toast buns cut-side down on the grate over the cooler side. Build and serve."],
tips=["Smash only once, right away. Pressing later squeezes out juice.","A cast iron press or a second spatula gives a thinner, crispier patty.","Scrape the plate between batches."]),"recipes",[("What temperature should smash burgers reach?","Ground beef should reach 160°F. Thin smash patties get there fast; check one with a thermometer.")])

page("chicken-thighs-on-a-collapsible-grill","Juicy Chicken Thighs on a Collapsible Grill","Boneless or bone-in chicken thighs on a flat pack charcoal grill using a two-zone fire, with a simple spice rub.","c08",recipe(
"<p>Chicken thighs are the most forgiving meat on a small charcoal grill. They stay juicy at higher temperatures and take on smoke and char beautifully. A two-zone fire keeps them from burning.</p>",
"3–4","40 minutes",["6 boneless skinless chicken thighs (or 4 bone-in)","1 tbsp oil","1 tsp salt","1 tsp smoked paprika","1 tsp garlic powder","½ tsp black pepper","½ tsp brown sugar (optional)"],
["Mix the spices. Pat the thighs dry, rub with oil, season all over.","Build a two-zone fire ({0}).".format(L("two-zone-fire-collapsible-grill","how")),"Preheat and oil the grates.","Sear the thighs over the coals 3 to 4 minutes per side until well marked.","Move to the cool side. Cook, turning occasionally, until 165°F at minimum. Many cooks take thighs to 175–185°F for the best texture.","Rest 5 minutes before slicing."],
tips=["Bone-in thighs take longer; start skin-side up on the cool side, then crisp the skin over the coals at the end.","If you use a sugary sauce, brush it on only during the last few minutes."]),"recipes",[("Can chicken thighs go above 165°F?","Yes. 165°F is the minimum safe temperature; thighs are often more tender at 175–185°F.")])

page("pork-tenderloin-on-a-collapsible-grill","Grilled Pork Tenderloin on a Collapsible Grill","A whole pork tenderloin seared over charcoal and finished on the cool side of a flat pack grill, to a safe and juicy 145°F.","c08",recipe(
"<p>Pork tenderloin fits a compact grill perfectly: long and slim, it cooks in about 20 minutes. The trick is pulling it at 145°F and resting it so it stays moist.</p>",
"3–4","35 minutes",["1 pork tenderloin, about 1–1¼ lb, silver skin trimmed","1 tbsp oil","1 tsp salt","1 tsp black pepper","1 tsp ground cumin or dried thyme","2 cloves garlic, minced"],
["Mix the seasonings with the oil and rub over the pork. Let sit 15 minutes while the fire lights.","Build a two-zone fire.","Sear on all sides over the coals, about 2 minutes per side, 8 minutes total.","Move to the cool side and cook, turning every few minutes, until the thickest part reads 145°F, about 8 to 12 more minutes.","Rest 3 minutes, then slice into medallions."],
tips=["The thin tail end cooks faster; keep it toward the cooler edge.","Lay it diagonally if it's too long for the cooking area."]),"recipes",[("Is pink pork safe at 145°F?","Yes. USDA's safe minimum for whole cuts of pork is 145°F with a 3-minute rest, and it may still look slightly pink.")])

page("griddle-breakfast-on-a-collapsible-grill","Griddle Breakfast on a Collapsible Grill","Bacon, eggs and potatoes on a carbon steel griddle plate over charcoal: a camp breakfast plan for a flat pack grill.","grid1",recipe(
"<p>A griddle plate makes a collapsible grill a breakfast machine. Bacon first, then potatoes in the drippings, then eggs.</p>",
"2–3","40 minutes",["6 slices bacon","2 medium potatoes, diced small and parboiled (or 2 cups frozen diced hash browns)","½ onion, diced","4–6 eggs","Salt, pepper","Tortillas or toast (optional)"],
["Light about half a chimney. Spread coals mostly under the griddle, a thinner layer under one end.","Preheat the griddle and lay the bacon on the cooler area. Cook, turning, until crisp. Set aside.","Push the drippings to the center. Add potatoes and onion; cook 10 to 15 minutes, turning occasionally, until crisp. Season.","Move potatoes aside. Add a little oil and crack the eggs onto the cooler part of the plate. Cook until whites and yolks are firm (or to 160°F for scrambled).","Warm tortillas on the grate side, wrap it all up."],
tips=["Parboiling potatoes at home cuts griddle time in half.","Keep the eggs on the cooler end to avoid scorching."]),"recipes",[])

page("chicken-and-vegetable-kebabs-collapsible-grill","Chicken and Vegetable Kebabs on a Collapsible Grill","Skewered chicken and vegetables sized to fit across a flat pack grill, with a lemon-garlic marinade.","c28",recipe(
"<p>Kebabs suit a long, narrow cooking area: lay skewers crosswise and you can fit a whole meal. Keep the chicken and vegetables on separate skewers so each cooks to its own timing.</p>",
"4","1 hour (incl. 30 min marinating)",["1½ lb boneless chicken breast or thigh, cut in 1¼&quot; cubes","Juice of 1 lemon, 3 tbsp olive oil, 2 cloves garlic, 1 tsp salt, 1 tsp oregano","1 red onion, 1 bell pepper, 1 zucchini, cut in chunks","Metal skewers, or wooden skewers soaked 30 minutes"],
["Marinate the chicken 30 minutes to 4 hours in the fridge. Toss vegetables in a little oil and salt.","Thread chicken and vegetables onto separate skewers. Discard used marinade.","Build a two-zone fire. Preheat and oil the grates.","Grill chicken skewers over the coals, turning every 2 to 3 minutes, until 165°F inside, about 10 to 12 minutes.","Grill vegetable skewers at the edge of the coals until tender and charred.","Rest briefly, then serve with rice, flatbread or salad."],
tips=["Skewer lengths that span the grill's short side (9&quot; on the Compact) lie flat and don't fall in.","Don't pack pieces tightly; space lets heat in."]),"recipes",[])

page("grilled-salmon-collapsible-grill","Grilled Salmon on a Collapsible Grill","Skin-on salmon fillets cooked over charcoal on a flat pack grill or griddle plate, with tips to stop sticking.","c08",recipe(
"<p>Salmon is quick over charcoal and easy if you avoid sticking. Skin-on fillets and a well-oiled grate (or a griddle plate) are the keys.</p>",
"2–3","25 minutes",["2–3 skin-on salmon fillets, about 6 oz each","1 tbsp oil","Salt, pepper","1 lemon","Optional: 1 tsp brown sugar and ½ tsp chili powder for a crust"],
["Pat the fillets very dry, oil them, season.","Build a two-zone fire, medium-hot. Clean and oil the grates thoroughly, or preheat a griddle plate.","Lay fillets skin-side down over the edge of the coals. Don't move them for 4 to 5 minutes.","When the skin releases easily, flip carefully onto the flesh side for 1 to 2 minutes, or leave skin-side down and move to the cool side to finish.","Cook to 145°F, or until the flesh is opaque and flakes with a fork.","Squeeze lemon over and serve."],
tips=["If it sticks, wait; it releases once the skin crisps.","The griddle is foolproof for delicate fish."]),"recipes",[])

page("grilled-fruit-dessert-collapsible-grill","Grilled Fruit Dessert on a Collapsible Grill","Pineapple, peaches and bananas grilled on the last coals of a flat pack grill, with simple toppings.","c28",recipe(
"<p>The fire is dying, dinner is done, and the grill is still hot enough for dessert. Grilled fruit caramelizes in minutes.</p>",
"4","15 minutes",["1 pineapple, cut in rings or spears (or canned rings, drained)","2 ripe peaches, halved and pitted","2 bananas, unpeeled, halved lengthwise","1 tbsp melted butter or oil","Cinnamon, honey, and ice cream or yogurt to serve"],
["Clean and oil the grates over the remaining coals.","Brush fruit with butter.","Grill pineapple and peaches cut-side down 2 to 4 minutes until marked, then turn.","Grill bananas cut-side down 2 minutes, then skin-side down until soft.","Serve warm with cinnamon, honey and ice cream."],
tips=["Sugar burns fast. Watch it.","Firm-ripe fruit holds its shape better than very soft fruit."]),"recipes",[])
